  "asr_text": "I welcomed them. A bad dream, I explained. The cry was mine. The old man was away in the country. I showed them every room, then brought chairs into his bedroom. I sat directly above the body. You see how little I feared? They chatted pleasantly. I smiled. Then my head began to ache. A ringing filled my ears. But no, that low quick beating again. I spoke louder. It grew louder too. I paced and scraped my chair across the boards. Still they chatted, still they smiled. Louder, louder. Could you have borne it? They heard, they knew. Their smiles were mocking me. I could bear no more. I did it, I screamed. Tear up the planks. Here, it is the beating of his hideous heart.",
